1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,870
7,900 euros: that's the price
of an RTX 5090, today.

2
00:00:04,160 --> 00:00:06,890
With it, Qwen runs at up to
75 tokens per second.

3
00:00:06,940 --> 00:00:09,830
On a 5060 Ti, its file
doesn't even fit.

4
00:00:09,900 --> 00:00:13,310
You have to take a more compressed
version, and then you drop to 28.

5
00:00:13,460 --> 00:00:17,910
Qwen 4, meanwhile, is only a preview
in Alibaba's cloud.

6
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:19,610
For now, there's nothing
to download,

7
00:00:19,660 --> 00:00:24,870
except the 5060 Ti and the 5080 have
already gone up more than 20% in a month.

8
00:00:25,040 --> 00:00:27,050
So, do you buy now,
or do you wait?

9
00:00:27,100 --> 00:00:30,430
Here's the ranking, card by card,
with today's prices.

10
00:00:30,480 --> 00:00:33,930
I'll show you what's certain about Qwen 4
and what isn't.

11
00:00:34,160 --> 00:00:37,630
The card for your budget, in euros,
and what the one you already have does.

12
00:00:37,720 --> 00:00:40,510
Along the way, there are 2 free settings
that nearly triple

13
00:00:40,560 --> 00:00:42,190
the speed of a pair of cards.

14
00:00:42,240 --> 00:00:46,410
And at the end, I answer your question
in one sentence: buy or wait.

15
00:00:46,700 --> 00:00:50,190
No, Qwen 4 can't be downloaded
from Qwen's official page.

16
00:00:50,240 --> 00:00:52,330
As I'm recording this,
there isn't one.

17
00:00:52,380 --> 00:00:55,430
But if you type "Qwen4-27B"
on Hugging Face,

18
00:00:55,640 --> 00:00:58,050
you'll land on pages
with that name.

19
00:00:58,240 --> 00:00:59,470
Open them, they're empty.

20
00:00:59,540 --> 00:01:03,490
In fact, people are just reserving
the spot for the day it's released.

21
00:01:03,720 --> 00:01:07,350
So if someone offers you a Qwen 4
to download today, be careful.

22
00:01:07,580 --> 00:01:10,910
As for me, I'm currently watching Qwen 4
for a simple reason.

23
00:01:11,200 --> 00:01:14,790
In August, Qwen released a preview,
Qwen 3.8 Flash Next,

24
00:01:14,860 --> 00:01:16,950
which shows Qwen 4's architecture.

25
00:01:17,100 --> 00:01:20,310
And in coding, according to Qwen's tests,
it already beats the 27B.

26
00:01:20,360 --> 00:01:23,150
So I'm expecting a lot from Qwen 4,
especially since Qwen

27
00:01:23,200 --> 00:01:25,870
is one of the most recommended families
for coding locally.

28
00:01:26,120 --> 00:01:28,610
What Alibaba has put in black and white
is very little.

29
00:01:28,740 --> 00:01:32,470
On September 22, its press release says
Qwen 4 is "in training,"

30
00:01:32,720 --> 00:01:33,870
with no date or size.

31
00:01:34,080 --> 00:01:35,730
And since November 11,

32
00:01:35,860 --> 00:01:40,590
a preview, Qwen 4 Max,
is open until November 25.

33
00:01:41,240 --> 00:01:44,050
But only in the cloud,
through the Alibaba subscription

34
00:01:44,100 --> 00:01:47,210
and early access in its apps,
like the Qwen app.

35
00:01:47,260 --> 00:01:49,150
You can try it,
but not download it.

36
00:01:49,500 --> 00:01:51,850
So here too,
we don't have a file yet.

37
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:53,630
And the 27-billion Qwen 4,

38
00:01:53,880 --> 00:01:55,830
the one you could run
at home,

39
00:01:55,900 --> 00:01:57,410
according to the Chinese press,

40
00:01:57,460 --> 00:02:01,410
was shown at the conference
as the open version of Qwen 4.

41
00:02:01,460 --> 00:02:03,890
Except Alibaba hasn't written it anywhere,

42
00:02:03,980 --> 00:02:06,190
not in its press release,
not in its documentation.

43
00:02:06,420 --> 00:02:08,310
We know neither its size,
nor its date,

44
00:02:08,360 --> 00:02:12,550
so for now it's an announced name
and nobody has seen its file.

45
00:02:12,680 --> 00:02:14,330
As for the rest, here's what people say:

46
00:02:14,380 --> 00:02:17,650
about 15 GB, estimated from
a piece of software's code,

47
00:02:17,700 --> 00:02:20,050
and a release "next week,"

48
00:02:20,360 --> 00:02:21,370
reported secondhand.

49
00:02:21,680 --> 00:02:25,650
But then, the 75 and the 28
from the start, what are they?

50
00:02:25,700 --> 00:02:27,710
It's Qwen 3.8, 27 billion:

51
00:02:27,900 --> 00:02:29,970
today's Qwen,
the one you can download.

52
00:02:30,100 --> 00:02:32,430
It's like freeing up space
on your SSD

53
00:02:32,480 --> 00:02:34,830
for a game nobody knows the size of.

54
00:02:34,940 --> 00:02:36,570
You take the previous one as a benchmark:

55
00:02:36,620 --> 00:02:38,770
if Qwen 4 keeps that size,
these numbers will hold,

56
00:02:38,820 --> 00:02:40,230
otherwise I redo the math.

57
00:02:40,360 --> 00:02:43,550
Its most common file, the Q4_K_M,
weighs 16.5 GB.

58
00:02:43,600 --> 00:02:46,810
And for it to run fast,
it has to fit on your card,

59
00:02:46,860 --> 00:02:50,010
with room to store
the conversation.

60
00:02:50,200 --> 00:02:53,530
Otherwise, part of it spills into RAM
and from then on, it lags.

61
00:02:53,580 --> 00:02:54,870
We start with 16 GB.

62
00:02:54,940 --> 00:02:59,370
With the RTX 5060 Ti, as you saw,
the Q4_K_M doesn't fit.

63
00:02:59,440 --> 00:03:01,730
So we take a tighter file
of 14 GB

64
00:03:01,780 --> 00:03:04,550
and a user measures
28 tokens per second.

65
00:03:04,600 --> 00:03:06,090
For chatting, that's very decent.

66
00:03:06,140 --> 00:03:09,310
On the other hand, you have less than 2 GB
left for the conversation.

67
00:03:09,420 --> 00:03:13,030
So for a coding agent that reads
whole files, it's really tight.

68
00:03:13,080 --> 00:03:16,110
I covered it all on Monday
in the video about 16 GB.

69
00:03:16,360 --> 00:03:18,750
On price, look closely:
the same card from the same brand

70
00:03:18,800 --> 00:03:22,230
costs 833 euros at Amazon
and 1,100 at LDLC.

71
00:03:22,280 --> 00:03:24,850
More than 250 euros of difference
for the same box.

72
00:03:25,140 --> 00:03:26,150
So compare before you pay:

73
00:03:26,200 --> 00:03:28,590
to try things out, it's enough,
for real work, it's tight.

74
00:03:28,640 --> 00:03:30,570
And used, there's much cheaper:

75
00:03:30,640 --> 00:03:34,010
a Radeon RX 6800 XT,
16 GB as well,

76
00:03:34,160 --> 00:03:36,450
around 280 euros on Leboncoin.

77
00:03:36,500 --> 00:03:41,130
Except I found no measurement
of this model on that card.

78
00:03:41,200 --> 00:03:42,850
So I can't give you a speed.

79
00:03:42,900 --> 00:03:46,770
Next tier: 24 GB,
with the RTX 3090.

80
00:03:46,820 --> 00:03:49,230
This time, the Q4_K_M fits

81
00:03:49,280 --> 00:03:52,190
and about 8 GB are left
for the conversation.

82
00:03:52,240 --> 00:03:54,950
Result: around 40 tokens
per second,

83
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:58,030
and still 34 when the conversation
gets very long.

84
00:03:58,080 --> 00:04:01,630
And here there's a setting
you're going to hear about: MTP.

85
00:04:01,680 --> 00:04:04,850
Basically, the model guesses several words
ahead, then checks them.

86
00:04:04,900 --> 00:04:09,830
On a 3090, a user goes from 40
to 70 tokens, on code.

87
00:04:09,880 --> 00:04:13,290
The gain drops as the conversation
gets longer, but it's free.

88
00:04:13,340 --> 00:04:18,130
New, the 3090 is still listed
at nearly 3,000 euros at Amazon.

89
00:04:18,180 --> 00:04:21,790
Obviously, nobody buys it new:
its real price is the used price.

90
00:04:21,840 --> 00:04:26,010
Today, on Leboncoin,
I see one at 850 euros,

91
00:04:26,060 --> 00:04:28,430
less than a third of the new price.

92
00:04:28,480 --> 00:04:31,570
But if you buy used, check
that it works before paying.

93
00:04:31,620 --> 00:04:35,050
On the AMD side,
there's the RX 7900 XTX,

94
00:04:35,100 --> 00:04:38,870
which also has 24 GB, for a little more
than 1,400 euros new.

95
00:04:38,920 --> 00:04:42,810
Except its measurements range
from 29 to 41 tokens per second,

96
00:04:42,860 --> 00:04:44,630
depending on the software and the system.

97
00:04:44,680 --> 00:04:47,250
So with it, it's less predictable.

98
00:04:47,300 --> 00:04:50,390
Now, the best tier
is the 32 GB one.

99
00:04:50,440 --> 00:04:52,390
First option, two 5060 Tis,

100
00:04:52,440 --> 00:04:55,090
and that's where the 2 free
settings are hiding.

101
00:04:55,140 --> 00:04:58,530
By default, the software splits the model
in 2, layer by layer,

102
00:04:58,580 --> 00:05:00,270
and one card waits for the other,

103
00:05:00,320 --> 00:05:02,910
so, 22 tokens per second.

104
00:05:02,960 --> 00:05:05,910
Turn on tensor split,
and both cards compute at the same time.

105
00:05:05,960 --> 00:05:07,810
That takes you up to 37.

106
00:05:07,860 --> 00:05:10,590
Then add MTP,
and now you hit 66.

107
00:05:10,640 --> 00:05:13,250
Almost triple, without spending
one extra euro.

108
00:05:13,300 --> 00:05:15,150
And these are measurements
from the same person,

109
00:05:15,200 --> 00:05:17,810
with the same file:
the comparison is clean.

110
00:05:17,860 --> 00:05:19,470
Be careful though,
tensor split

111
00:05:19,520 --> 00:05:22,210
is still marked experimental
in the software.

112
00:05:22,260 --> 00:05:26,790
The 2 cards at Amazon will cost you
about 1,670 euros.

113
00:05:26,840 --> 00:05:30,590
Second option, the simplest:
one RTX 5090,

114
00:05:30,640 --> 00:05:34,050
up to 75 tokens per second,
without even MTP.

115
00:05:34,100 --> 00:05:36,430
So with equal settings,
it stays ahead.

116
00:05:36,480 --> 00:05:39,210
Except in stock,
it starts at 7,900 euros,

117
00:05:39,260 --> 00:05:41,750
and its median price has almost doubled
in 3 months.

118
00:05:41,800 --> 00:05:44,550
So for the price of one 5090,

119
00:05:44,600 --> 00:05:47,110
you could buy almost 5 pairs of 5060s.

120
00:05:47,160 --> 00:05:48,490
Well, you don't need 5,

121
00:05:48,540 --> 00:05:52,210
but I'm making a whole video
on 32 GB next week.

122
00:05:52,260 --> 00:05:53,750
And if you're not in France,

123
00:05:53,800 --> 00:05:55,510
maybe you can get it
cheaper where you are,

124
00:05:55,560 --> 00:05:57,510
but I'm keeping prices
in euros

125
00:05:57,560 --> 00:05:59,690
and you convert to your currency.

126
00:05:59,740 --> 00:06:02,830
And at the end, also tell me
how much it can cost where you are.

127
00:06:03,240 --> 00:06:04,770
And if you already have a card, then

128
00:06:04,820 --> 00:06:07,890
before buying anything,
just check whether the file fits.

129
00:06:07,940 --> 00:06:10,750
With 16 GB, it works
with the tighter file, as we saw.

130
00:06:10,860 --> 00:06:13,450
And with MTP,
the 5060 Ti user

131
00:06:13,500 --> 00:06:16,530
goes from 28 to 51
on a short conversation.

132
00:06:16,600 --> 00:06:20,110
On a 5080, someone measured
101 tokens per second,

133
00:06:20,160 --> 00:06:24,110
even with the 3-bit file, less precise,
and it's a single measurement.

134
00:06:24,260 --> 00:06:28,390
With 12 GB, on the other hand, this model
doesn't fit, even in 4 bits.

135
00:06:28,800 --> 00:06:30,070
Part of it goes into RAM.

136
00:06:30,140 --> 00:06:33,710
So on a 3060, you drop
to between 5 and 7 tokens per second.

137
00:06:33,860 --> 00:06:35,450
With 8 GB, it's worse.

138
00:06:35,520 --> 00:06:37,350
And that's the case for a lot of people.

139
00:06:37,420 --> 00:06:41,230
On Steam, in October, more than 1 player
in 4 had 8 GB,

140
00:06:41,460 --> 00:06:43,510
and about 1 player in 8 has 12.

141
00:06:43,580 --> 00:06:44,870
And the trap here is the price:

142
00:06:44,920 --> 00:06:49,750
a used 12 GB 3060, I see it for
between 280 and 320 euros on Leboncoin.

143
00:06:49,960 --> 00:06:51,930
Roughly the price of the 16 GB Radeon.

144
00:06:52,120 --> 00:06:55,310
So for this kind of model,
at the same price, take the 16.

145
00:06:55,360 --> 00:06:59,130
So if that's you,
Qwen 4 probably won't change anything.

146
00:06:59,180 --> 00:07:01,130
Nothing says it will be smaller,

147
00:07:01,180 --> 00:07:03,450
and for a model this size,

148
00:07:03,500 --> 00:07:05,910
you'll need a card
from the earlier tiers.

149
00:07:05,960 --> 00:07:08,570
So, do you buy now
or do you wait?

150
00:07:08,620 --> 00:07:10,890
First, waiting for Qwen 4
doesn't protect you from prices.

151
00:07:10,940 --> 00:07:12,770
They started going up without it.

152
00:07:12,820 --> 00:07:15,570
The cause put forward,
according to an American channel,

153
00:07:15,620 --> 00:07:16,750
is a memory shortage.

154
00:07:16,800 --> 00:07:19,250
And nobody knows
when it will come back down.

155
00:07:19,300 --> 00:07:22,710
But buying for Qwen 4 means buying
for a file nobody has seen.

156
00:07:22,760 --> 00:07:25,950
In fact, the 27B, meaning
the 27 billion,

157
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:28,290
was shown at a conference,
nothing more.

158
00:07:28,340 --> 00:07:31,470
But we do know one thing:
a 27-billion model in 4 bits

159
00:07:31,520 --> 00:07:34,690
weighs between 14 and 18 GB
depending on the file.

160
00:07:34,740 --> 00:07:36,670
We just saw it with Qwen 3.8.

161
00:07:36,720 --> 00:07:38,470
So if Qwen 4 keeps that size,

162
00:07:38,700 --> 00:07:42,310
24 GB keeps some margin
and 16 GB stays tight.

163
00:07:42,520 --> 00:07:43,570
So here's the rule.

164
00:07:43,620 --> 00:07:45,690
In one sentence:
don't buy for a name,

165
00:07:45,740 --> 00:07:49,350
buy for the size of a file,
plus room for the conversation.

166
00:07:49,400 --> 00:07:54,730
Today, that means about 24 GB
or 2x16 with the right setting.

167
00:07:54,840 --> 00:07:57,690
And if you already have 16 GB or more,
don't change anything for now,

168
00:07:57,860 --> 00:07:59,890
wait to see the real file.

169
00:08:00,040 --> 00:08:03,270
The day it comes out, I'll redo
this ranking with the real numbers.

170
00:08:03,460 --> 00:08:05,550
Me, I'm going to wait, because
projects like Strata

171
00:08:05,600 --> 00:08:08,310
already run a compressed version
of Flash Next,

172
00:08:08,460 --> 00:08:12,930
the preview of Qwen 4,
with 16 GB of VRAM and 32 GB of RAM.

173
00:08:12,980 --> 00:08:16,990
So if Qwen 4 keeps the same architecture,
maybe my 16 GB will be enough.

174
00:08:17,040 --> 00:08:19,390
So, tell me in the comments
which card you have

175
00:08:19,440 --> 00:08:21,570
and how much it really costs
where you are.

176
00:08:21,620 --> 00:08:22,890
I'll compile your answers,

177
00:08:22,940 --> 00:08:24,750
especially for those who don't have
access to French prices.

178
00:08:24,800 --> 00:08:25,910
And if you have 16 GB,

179
00:08:25,960 --> 00:08:29,030
next week's video
tells you which file to take.

180
00:08:29,080 --> 00:08:30,730
So, see you next time,

181
00:08:30,780 --> 00:08:34,790
and next week, I'll test
the Strata version on 16 GB,

182
00:08:34,840 --> 00:08:38,150
and I'll also explain how
32 GB of VRAM works, in detail.

183
00:08:38,200 --> 00:08:39,200
Alright, bye!
